{
  "slug": "openregistry",
  "name": "Openregistry",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Live, government-identical company data from 27 national registries in one install — MCP server + 10 Skills + 6 slash commands. Walk cross-border ownership chains, run KYC/AML due diligence, detect shell companies, pull live XBRL financial statements, monitor corporate filings, check global name availability. Every response is byte-identical to what UK Companies House, France RNE, Germany Handelsregister, Korea OpenDART, Canada CBCA, 10 US state registries, and more return — no aggregator markup, no stale cache. A platform by Sophymarine.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 skills**, **6 commands** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (5): `find-company` (Verify a specific company exists in its national government registry and capture its core identity: current status (active…), `get-director-details` (Retrieve the current and historical officers of a known company — directors, secretaries, board members, partners, with roles,…), `get-filings` (Retrieve the filing history of a known company — every document the company has filed with its national…), `get-financials` (Pull the most recent annual accounts of a known company and extract the headline financial figures: revenue /…), `get-shareholder-details` (Retrieve the registered shareholders, members, or quota-holders of a known company — the statutory equity roster as published…)\n- **Commands** (6): `accounts` (Pull the most recent statutory financial statements from the government registry and extract key figures (revenue, operating profit,…), `dd` (Run a full statutory due-diligence dossier on a company using OpenRegistry), `filings` (Scan recent filings on a company and surface material events (director changes, new charges, capital events, insolvency markers)), `name` (Check whether a proposed company name is free to register across multiple government registers — live, direct), `shellcheck` (Score shell-company probability from 10 live signals (single director, zero filed accounts, overseas office, nominee-director pattern, PSC=director overlap,…), `ubo` (Walk the cross-border ownership chain of a company until you reach individuals, listed entities, or an AML gate)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `openregistry`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install openregistry@claude-community` from `sophymarine/openregistry`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
